A||||8||ezsurf||Ball Joints||||5||
Z||000000||ezsurf||05-03-2000||08:17 PM||||How can you tell if your ball joints are wore out?  Specifically, the rear ball joints.||||reg||5
Z||000001||geyser||05-03-2000||09:38 PM||||It hurts when you walk.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||05-03-2000||09:46 PM||||Hahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha<P>hahahahahahahahahahahah<BR>Damn that was funny!||||reg||1
Z||000003||ezsurf||05-03-2000||10:05 PM||||Sounds like your speaking from experience.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||05-04-2000||12:05 AM||||It helps if you have someone to help you. Elevate the wheel(s) in question and have someone rock the wheel holding it in the 6 o'clock and 12 o'clock position while you look underneath for movement in worn parts.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||05-04-2000||03:31 PM||||Jack up the car enough so the wheel just clears the ground. Put the jack handle under the tire and try lifting the tire. If you hear or feel a clunk or notice movement in the suspension parts, the ball joints are likely bad.<P>I've had a problem where they are bad but it was hard to get enough pressure or movement on them to see the loose-ness.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ezsurf||05-04-2000||09:34 PM||||Ozzy; Terryk - thanks for the input. I'm on the road right now, but I will check it out when I get home in a couple of weeks. - ez||||reg||1
